  "body": "## Summary\n- Adds independent SCAN engine v0.27 with a generic Qt QEvent::FileOpen to containing ^[vent(...) route correction.\n- Adds a regression test and retains SCAN's strict boundary: it is independent under Anchor/, not part of the MantleOS2 product; Hermes remains reference/example-only.\n- Moves SCAN governance, protocol, report, and roadmap into tracked Anchor/docs/ and makes the public README repository-relative with no personal Drive references.\n\n## Evidence\n- v0.27 full suite: 145 passed, 3 expected Windows symlink privilege skips.\n- Two cold manifest scans matched byte-for-byte across emitted artifacts and their canonical tables.\n- Warm-cache proof: 4,186 hits, 0 misses; canonical tables and cache-independent outputs matched.\n- Clean-package qualification passed (83/83 package files, LLM-disabled mechanical check, 12/12 acceptance queries).\n\n## Scope\nThis is a tested calibration candidate, not a frozen v0.27 release. The separate Python 3.13 installed-wheel certification was intentionally stopped before completion to publish this branch now; no incomplete certification artifact is included.",
